  "question": {
    "text": "At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, the following equilibrium is established as<br />\r<math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>F</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>g</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>⇌</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>F</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>g</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math><br />\rThe composition of equilibrium may be determined by measuring the rate of effusion of the mixture through a pin hole. It is found that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math> mixture effuses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.6</mo></math> times as fast as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> effuses under the similar conditions. (At. wt. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn></math>). What is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math> (in atm) ?"
  },
